{#
calendar/_event_details.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
An event, read rather than edited.

Everything an event knows and nothing to fill in. Until this existed the only
way to look at one was the editor, so "when is this, and why is it on my
calendar?" was answered by opening a form that asks you to change it — and a
field with no answer showed as an empty input rather than being absent, which
reads as missing data instead of as no data.

Three things here are not on the form at all, because the form does not edit
them: the DESCRIPTION and the PARTICIPANTS, which live in the JSCalendar
overlay, and the PROVENANCE — the message this event was read out of. The last
is the one worth opening a dialog for. An extracted event is a guess a program
made about somebody's mail, and a guess you cannot trace is one you cannot
check.

Accepts:
  event         CalendarEvent
  title         string            — the instance's title where one differs
  startsAt      DateTimeImmutable — already in displayZone
  endsAt        DateTimeImmutable — already in displayZone
  timeZone      string|null       — the event's own zone, shown when it has one
  displayZone   string|false      — false for all-day; see the controller
  recurrenceId  string|null
  source        Message|null      — newest APPLIED claim, not the first
  returnTo      string|null

The mail link carries `data-turbo-frame="_top"`, or Turbo reads it as a
navigation of the modal frame and loads the whole mailbox inside the dialog —
the same trap _happening_soon.html.twig documents, and the reason its
provenance link carries it too.
#}
{% set jscal = event.jscalendar|default({}) %}
{% set description = jscal.description|default('')|trim %}
{% set participants = jscal.participants|default({}) %}

<turbo-frame id="modal" class="flex-1 min-h-0 flex flex-col">
    <div class="flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto px-6 pb-5 space-y-5">

        {# ── What and when ──────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="mt-0.5 flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg"
                  style="background-color: {{ event.calendar.color }}1a; color: {{ event.calendar.color }}">
                <i class="fa-regular fa-calendar text-sm" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </span>

            <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink break-words">
                    {{ title ?: 'calendar.soon.untitled'|trans }}
                </h2>

                {# The last day the event actually covers.
                   An all-day event is STORED with an exclusive end — midnight
                   on the day AFTER the last one — so the day a reader would
                   name is one before it. Same conversion the toolbar makes for
                   its range label, see _toolbar_shell.html.twig. A timed event
                   ends when it says it does. #}
                {% set lastDay = event.isAllDay ? endsAt|date_modify('-1 day') : endsAt %}
                {% set spansDays = startsAt|date('Y-m-d', displayZone)
                                != lastDay|date('Y-m-d', displayZone) %}

                <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">
                    {%- if spansDays %}
                        {# BOTH ends, because one date and two times reads as an
                           hour. A Friday-to-Sunday festival was printed here as
                           "Friday 28 August · 15:00 – 16:00" — the start day,
                           the start time and the end time of a different day —
                           which is a one-hour event on the wrong scale, while
                           the grid beside it drew the span correctly. #}
                        {{ startsAt|intl_date('EEEE d MMMM', displayZone) }}
                        {%- if not event.isAllDay %} · {{ startsAt|date(clock.time, displayZone) }}{% endif %}
                        – {{ lastDay|intl_date('EEEE d MMMM', displayZone) }}
                        {%- if not event.isAllDay %} · {{ endsAt|date(clock.time, displayZone) }}
                        {%- else %} · {{ 'calendar.event.all_day'|trans }}
                        {%- endif %}
                    {%- else %}
                        {{ startsAt|intl_date('EEEE d MMMM', displayZone) }}
                        {%- if not event.isAllDay %}
                            · {{ startsAt|date(clock.time, displayZone) }} – {{ endsAt|date(clock.time, displayZone) }}
                        {%- else %}
                            · {{ 'calendar.event.all_day'|trans }}
                        {%- endif %}
                    {%- endif %}
                </p>

                {# Only when the event carries its own zone. Printing the
                   reader's would say nothing — it is the clock everything else
                   on the page is already on. #}
                {% if timeZone is not empty and not event.isAllDay %}
                    <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-ink-faint">{{ timeZone }}</p>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        </div>

        {# ── The facts it has ───────────────────────────────────────────── #}
        <dl class="space-y-3 text-sm">
            {% if event.location is not empty %}
                <div class="flex gap-3">
                    <dt class="w-24 shrink-0 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-faint pt-0.5">
                        {{ 'calendar.event.location'|trans }}
                    </dt>
                    <dd class="min-w-0 flex-1 text-ink break-words">{{ event.location }}</dd>
                </div>
            {% endif %}

            <div class="flex gap-3">
                <dt class="w-24 shrink-0 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-faint pt-0.5">
                    {{ 'calendar.event.calendar'|trans }}
                </dt>
                <dd class="min-w-0 flex-1 flex items-center gap-2 text-ink">
                    <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 shrink-0 rounded-full"
                          style="background-color: {{ event.calendar.color }}"></span>
                    <span class="truncate">{{ event.calendar.name }}</span>
                </dd>
            </div>

            {% if event.isRecurring %}
                <div class="flex gap-3">
                    <dt class="w-24 shrink-0 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-faint pt-0.5">
                        {{ 'calendar.event.repeats'|trans }}
                    </dt>
                    <dd class="min-w-0 flex-1 text-ink">
                        {{ 'calendar.details.recurring'|trans }}
                        {%- if event.recurrenceUntil %}
                            · {{ 'calendar.details.until'|trans({
                                '%date%': event.recurrenceUntil|intl_date('d MMM yyyy', displayZone),
                            }) }}
                        {%- endif %}
                    </dd>
                </div>
            {% endif %}

            {% if event.myParticipation is not null %}
                <div class="flex gap-3">
                    <dt class="w-24 shrink-0 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-faint pt-0.5">
                        {{ 'calendar.details.your_answer'|trans }}
                    </dt>
                    {# calendar.invite.status.*, not a new set: those labels
                       already exist and are already translated three ways. The
                       key uses underscores where the enum value uses a hyphen
                       (RFC 8984 spells it "needs-action"), so the value is
                       normalised rather than the catalogue being reshaped. #}
                    <dd class="min-w-0 flex-1 text-ink">
                        {{ ('calendar.invite.status.' ~ event.myParticipation.value|replace({'-': '_'}))|trans }}
                    </dd>
                </div>
            {% endif %}

            {# Status only when it is NOT the ordinary one. "Confirmed" on every
               event is a row that never varies, and a detail view that lists
               constants buries the things that do change. #}
            {% if event.status.value != 'confirmed' %}
                <div class="flex gap-3">
                    <dt class="w-24 shrink-0 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-faint pt-0.5">
                        {{ 'calendar.details.status'|trans }}
                    </dt>
                    <dd class="min-w-0 flex-1 text-ink">
                        {{ ('calendar.status.' ~ event.status.value)|trans }}
                    </dd>
                </div>
            {% endif %}
        </dl>

        {# ── Participants ───────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
        {% if participants is not empty %}
            <div>
                <h3 class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-faint">
                    {{ 'calendar.details.participants'|trans }}
                </h3>

                <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5">
                    {% for key, person in participants %}
                        {% set person_email = person.email|default(key) %}
                        {% set person_name = person.name|default('')|trim %}
                        <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm min-w-0">
                            <i class="fa-regular fa-user text-[11px] text-ink-faint shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            <span class="truncate text-ink">{{ person_name ?: person_email }}</span>
                            {% if person_name and person_email %}
                                <span class="truncate text-xs text-ink-faint">{{ person_email }}</span>
                            {% endif %}
                        </li>
                    {% endfor %}
                </ul>
            </div>
        {% endif %}

        {# ── Description ────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
        {% if description is not empty %}
            <div>
                <h3 class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-faint">
                    {{ 'calendar.details.description'|trans }}
                </h3>
                {# whitespace-pre-line: a description arrives with real newlines
                   and HTML collapses them. Escaped, never raw — this text came
                   off somebody's mail. #}
                <p class="mt-2 whitespace-pre-line break-words text-sm text-ink-soft">{{ description }}</p>
            </div>
        {% endif %}

        {# ── Where it came from ─────────────────────────────────────────── #}
        {% if source is not null %}
            <div class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-sunken/40 p-3">
                <h3 class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-faint">
                    {{ 'calendar.details.provenance'|trans }}
                </h3>

                <a href="{{ path('app_mail_message', { id: source.id }) }}"
                   data-turbo-frame="_top"
                   class="mt-2 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-accent hover:underline min-w-0">
                    <i class="fa-regular fa-envelope text-xs shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="truncate">{{ source.subject ?: 'calendar.soon.untitled'|trans }}</span>
                </a>

                {% if event.isExtracted %}
                    <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-ink-faint">{{ 'calendar.details.extracted_hint'|trans }}</p>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        {% endif %}
    </div>

    {# ── Edit, one step in ──────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <div class="shrink-0 border-t border-line px-6 py-3 flex justify-end">
        <a href="{{ path('app_calendar_event_edit', {
               id: event.id,
               instance: recurrenceId,
               returnTo: returnTo,
           })|trim('?') }}"
           data-turbo-frame="modal"
           class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 h-9 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium
                  bg-accent hover:bg-accent-strong text-accent-ink transition-colors">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-pen text-[11px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            {{ 'calendar.details.edit'|trans }}
        </a>
    </div>
</turbo-frame>
